    "description": "Returns an inbound email as text a person or a model can read: the words of the message in reading order, without markup, hidden content, link targets or the quoted history below a reply. For a marketing email this can be a hundred times smaller than the record from `GET /emails/{id}`, which you still need for the stored bodies, headers, authentication results or delivery state.\n\nEach link is a `[n]` marker beside its label. `link_count` says how many there are; ask for targets with `links`.\n\nA long body comes in pages of at most `max_chars` characters, ending on a line break where one is in reach. When `body_next_offset` is not null, send it as `offset` to read on.\n\nThe access rules of `GET /emails/{id}` apply. When content is withheld (for example a sender your filter blocked), the identifying fields are returned with an empty `body_text` and a `body_source` of `none`.",
