              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ],
              "maxLength": 200,
              "description": "A plain-text preview of `body_text` (never `body_html`), computed once when the message is stored: quoted replies (an \"On ... wrote:\" line, an \"Original Message\" separator, a From/Sent header block, `>` lines) and a `-- ` signature are cut off, whitespace is collapsed to single spaces, and the result is at most 200 characters. A message with no text body, or with nothing left once quotes and the signature are cut (a quote-only reply), has no snippet. It is not a summary and may end mid-word; read the full body from the detail endpoint. Null when the send has no text body or its content was discarded."
