    "binaryResponse": false,
    "bodyRequired": true,
    "command": "signal-email",
    "description": "Builds and sends the standard signal email about this received email: one `interaction.json` part (read/1, working/1 or typing/1 naming the email's Message-ID) plus only the fixed fallback text, threaded to it. It goes only to the email's authenticated sender, never to Reply-To or other recipients. Receivers see it as `fyi: true`, and the sender sees it as `peer_signal_on_my_last` (typing is not reported there). Refused (422) for a signal, interaction or other structured email, for an unauthenticated sender, and while the email is still being processed. Each call is a new signal with fresh ids; a read retried with the same Idempotency-Key rebuilds the identical message and dedupes.",
    "hasJsonBody": true,
